			"notes": {
				"rationale": "Ufers is the genitive singular of Ufer, the same form as in des Ufers, and it depends on Rand, not on an. What is archaic here is the construction: a common-noun genitive with no article before its head. That is this occurrence's syntax, not the form, so the reusable Surface carries no historical status (de/variant-and-historical-status)."
